<td align="center">6</td><td align="center">5</td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">3</td><td align="center">3</td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">Ns</td></tr><tr><td align="left">&#x02003;Hand rash</td><td align="center">4</td><td align="center">4</td><td align="center">5</td><td align="center">5</td><td align="center">6</td><td align="center">6</td><td align="center">6</td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">Ns</td></tr><tr><td align="left">&#x02003;Pimples</td><td align="center">4</td><td align="center">5</td><td align="center">6</td><td align="center">7</td><td align="center">8</td><td align="center">17</td><td align="center">9</td><td align="center">5</td><td align="center">&#x0003c; 0.001</td></tr><tr><td align="left">&#x02003;Face rash</td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">7</td><td align="center">3</td><td align="center">3</td><td align="center">6</td><td align="center">4</td><td align="center">5</td><td align="center">&#x0003c; 0.001</td></tr><tr><td align="left">&#x02003;Warts</td><td align="center">1</td><td align="center">1</td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">1</td><td align="center">9</td><td align="center">6</td><td align="center">0</td><td align="center">&#x0003c; 0.001</td></tr><tr><td align="left">&#x02003;Sweat</td><td align="center">4</td><td align="center">4</td><td align="center">16</td><td align="center">7</td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">11</td><td align="center">16</td><td align="center">4</td><td align="center">&#x0003c; 0.001</td></tr><tr><td align="left">&#x02003;Hair loss</td><td align="center">3</td><td align="center">3</td><td align="center">14</td><td align="center">31</td><td align="center">14</td><td align="center">20</td><td align="center">29</td><td align="center">7</td><td align="center">&#x0003c; 0.001</td></tr><tr><td align="left">&#x02003;Other skin complaints</td><td align="center">3</td><td align="center">3</td><td align="center">9</td><td align="center">3</td><td align="center">4</td><td align="center">6</td><td align="center">12</td><td align="center">0</td><td align="center">&#x0003c; 0.001</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><p>** Level of significance between the ethnic groups.</p></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></sec><sec><title>Pre-publication history</title><p>The pre-publication history for this paper can be accessed here:</p><p><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.biomedcentral.com/1471-5945/7/4/prepub"/></p></sec></body><back><ack><sec><title>Acknowledgements</title><p>Special thanks to Ingvild Dalen, statistician, for useful comments.</p><p>This study has been financed from the Norwegian Foundation for Health and Rehabilitation. The data collection was conducted as part of the Oslo Health Study 2000-2001 in collaboration with the National Health Screening Service of Norway &#x02013; now the Norwegian Institute of Public Health.</p></sec></ack><ref-list><ref id="B1"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Macbeth</surname><given-names>HP</given-names><suffix>S</suffix></name></person-group><source>Health and Ethnicity</source><year>2001</year><volume>Chapter 4</volume><publisher-name>London and New York , Taylor and Francis</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B2"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bhopal</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Glossary of terms relating to ethnicity and race: for reflection and debate</article-title><source>Journal of Epidemiology &#x00026; Community Health 58(6):441-5</source><year>2004</year></citation></ref><ref id="B3"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bhopal</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Donaldson</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>White, European, Western, Caucasian, or what? Inappropriate labeling in research on race, ethnicity, and health</article-title><source>American Journal of Public Health</source><year>1998</year><volume>88</volume><fpage>1303</fpage><lpage>1307</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9736867</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B4"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bhopal</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Rankin</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Concepts and terminology in ethnicity, race and health: be aware of the ongoing debate</article-title><source>British Dental Journal 186(10):483-4</source><year>1999</year></citation></ref><ref id="B5"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Senior</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name><name><surname>Bhopal</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ethnicity as a variable in epidemiological research.</article-title><source>British Medical Journal; 309(6950):327-30</source><year>1994</year></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fitzpatrick</surname><given-names>TB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The validity and practicality of sun-reactive skin types I through VI</article-title><source>Archives of Dermatology 124(6):869-71</source><year>1988</year></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Williams</surname><given-names>HC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Have you ever seen an Asian/Pacific Islander?</article-title><source>Archives of Dermatology</source><year>2002</year><volume>138</volume><fpage>673</fpage><lpage>674</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12020231</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1001/archderm.138.5.673</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rook</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Burns T, Breathnach S, Cox N, Griffiths C</surname></name></person-group><source>Rook's Textbook of Dermatology.</source><year>2004</year><publisher-name>Malden, MA. , Blackwell Science.</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Taylor</surname><given-names>SC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Skin of color: biology, structure, function, and implications for dermatologic disease. </article-title><source>Journal of the American Academy of Dermatology 46(2):S41-62</source><year>2002</year></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Child</surname><given-names>FJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Fuller</surname><given-names>LC</given-names></name><name><surname>Higgins</surname><given-names>EM</given-names></name><name><surname>Du Vivier</surname><given-names>AW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A study of the spectrum of skin disease occurring in a black population in south-east London</article-title><source>British Journal of Dermatology</source><year>1999</year><volume>141</volume><fpage>512</fpage><lpage>517</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10583057</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1365-2133.1999.03047.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Moy</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>McKinley-Grant</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Sanchez</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cultural aspects in the treatment of patients with skin disease.</article-title><source>Dermatologic Cli